Use case: identity-preserve. Asset type: separated animation parts texture atlas for Salve in FRONT THREE-QUARTER toward image-right. Reference1 is the exact original character identity and costume. Reference2 is her eight-view turnaround; choose ONLY the requested FRONT THREE-QUARTER toward image-right orientation consistently for EVERY piece. Soft original anime style, white hair, turquoise accents, black dress and white puff sleeves. Transparent alpha background.
Create one clean landscape 4-column by 2-row atlas, exactly8isolated pieces, each inside its own equalcell with transparentmargin. No grid lines, captions, numbers or text. Pieces in row-major order:
1 complete head with face only if visible from requested view, bangs and short framing hair (no body);
2 complete rear curtain of long white hair, reconstructing hidden hair surfaces (no face);
3 original black sleeveless bodice, white collar, bow and waist belt, continuing a small overlap into skirt (no sleeves);
4 complete original black/turquoise skirt as separate garment, including hidden waistband;
5 complete white sleeve and relaxed hand on character's left side, with rounded shoulder overlap; show its projection in requestedview even if it normally hides behindbody;
6 matching right sleeve and hand, consistentrequestedview;
7 left original black/turquoise boot, wholeboot only;
8 right original black/turquoise boot, wholeboot only.
Keep identifiable construction consistent with the original costume. No bare torso, no extra bodies or limbs, no alternate costumes or accessories. Natural anatomy of hands, fine clean edges and softshading. This is a parts atlas, not a finished combinedcharacter. Fully fill hidden garmentseams under layers so pieces canoverlap whenrigged. Keep two boots distinct and in same orientation. Parts may be scaled individually tofit cells; exactassemblyplacement will be calibrated separately. Output realRGBA transparency, not checkerboardpattern or backgroundglow.

